# AI Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define safe, useful AI features for legal workflows
- Protect client-attorney privilege and PII in AI interactions
- Standardize prompt engineering, streaming, and error handling

## Best Practices

- **AI as assistant, not authority** — always label AI-generated content
- **Human review required** for AI-drafted legal documents before sending
- **No PII in prompts** without explicit user consent and redaction
- **Streaming responses** for long-form generation (SSE or AI SDK)
- **Vercel AI SDK** for unified provider interface
- **Prompt templates** versioned in `services/ai/prompts/`
- **Token limits** enforced; truncate context intelligently
- **Audit log** all AI interactions with userId, feature, timestamp

## Planned AI Features (Roadmap)

| Feature | Phase | Description |
|---------|-------|-------------|
| Case summary | M4 | Summarize case notes and documents |
| Document draft | M5 | Template-based document generation |
| Deadline extraction | M5 | Parse documents for dates/deadlines |
| Smart search | M4 | Natural language case/client search |
| Email draft | M6 | Draft client communication |

## Coding Standards

```typescript
// AI service pattern
export class AiService {
  async summarizeCase(caseId: string, userId: string): Promise<ActionResult<string>> {
    await requirePermission(session, 'ai:use');
    const context = await this.buildSanitizedContext(caseId); // strip PII
    const result = await generateText({ model, prompt: SUMMARIZE_PROMPT, context });
    await auditLog.create({ action: 'AI_SUMMARIZE', entityId: caseId, userId });
    return { success: true, data: result.text };
  }
}
```

## Folder Structure

```
src/services/ai/
├── ai.service.ts
├── prompts/
│   ├── summarize-case.ts
│   └── draft-document.ts
├── sanitizers/
│   └── pii-redactor.ts
└── types.ts
src/features/ai/ui/          # AI feature UI components
```

## Naming Convention

- Prompt files: `{action}-{entity}.ts` → `summarize-case.ts`
- AI components: `Ai*` prefix → `AiSummaryPanel`
- Feature flags: `AI_{FEATURE}_ENABLED`

## Performance Rules

- Cache AI summaries until source data changes (hash-based invalidation)
- Stream responses >500 tokens
- Timeout AI calls at 30s with graceful fallback
- Queue long-running AI jobs (Phase 3)

## Security Rules

- **Never send privileged content to AI without firm policy consent**
- Redact SSN, account numbers, addresses before API calls
- AI API keys server-side only
- Log prompts/responses encrypted, retention 90 days max
- Allow firm admin to disable AI features entirely
- Comply with bar association AI usage guidelines (disclaimer in UI)

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — AI disclaimer UI
<Alert variant="info">
  <Sparkles className="h-4 w-4" />
  AI-generated content requires attorney review before use.
</Alert>

// ❌ BAD — Auto-send AI draft to client without review step
await sendEmail({ body: aiGeneratedDraft });
```

## Things to Avoid

- Fully automated legal advice to clients
- Training on client data without consent
- Storing AI API keys in client bundle
- Unbounded context windows (cost + privacy risk)
- Presenting AI output as verified legal fact

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] AI output labeled as AI-generated
- [ ] PII sanitized before external API call
- [ ] Permission check (`ai:use`) enforced
- [ ] Audit log entry created
- [ ] Human review step in UX flow
- [ ] Feature flag for rollout control
- [ ] Error/fallback UI when AI unavailable
